# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the Constrained Quantum Optimizer by Aqarios, you can solve constrained binary optimization problems on IBM&reg; quantum hardware without manual reformulation and circuit mapping. Simply supply a problem as an LP file, an MPS file, or a [Luna Model](https://docs.aqarios.com/luna-model). The function handles reformulation, circuit synthesis, transpilation, and hardware execution automatically. The solver utilizes iterative warm-starting [\\[1\\]](#references) of the [FlexQAOA](https://docs.aqarios.com/luna-solve/algorithms/quantum-gate/flexqaoa/) algorithm, a constraint-native extension of the Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA).\n"
msgstr "Sa Constrained Quantum Optimizer ni Aqarios, malulutas mo ang mga constrained binary optimization problem sa IBM&reg; quantum hardware nang walang manual reformulation at circuit mapping. Sapat nang magbigay ng problema bilang LP file, MPS file, o [Luna Model](https://docs.aqarios.com/luna-model). Awtomatikong hinahawakan ng function ang reformulation, circuit synthesis, transpilation, at hardware execution. Ginagamit ng solver ang iterative warm-starting [\\[1\\]](#references) ng [FlexQAOA](https://docs.aqarios.com/luna-solve/algorithms/quantum-gate/flexqaoa/) algorithm, isang constraint-native extension ng Quantum Approximate Optimization Algorithm (QAOA).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimizer targets binary problems with constraints. In particular, one-hot constraints and set-packing constraints can be natively enforced by using XY-mixers. Other constraint types are automatically reformulated as penalty terms.\n"
msgstr "Tinatarget ng optimizer ang mga binary problem na may constraints. Sa partikular, ang one-hot constraints at set-packing constraints ay maaaring i-enforce nang natively gamit ang XY-mixers. Ang ibang uri ng constraint ay awtomatikong nire-reformulate bilang penalty terms.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description {#description}"
msgstr "Deskripsyon {#description}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Disclaimer\">\n"
"Performance can depend on both the problem instance and subsequent processing steps. In some cases, classical samples and quantum-generated samples might achieve similar final solution quality after equivalent post-processing. Evaluation should therefore consider the complete optimization workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Paalala\">\n"
"Maaaring depende ang performance sa parehong problem instance at sa mga susunod na processing step. Sa ilang kaso, ang classical samples at quantum-generated samples ay maaaring magkaroon ng magkatulad na final solution quality matapos ang equivalent post-processing. Kaya dapat isaalang-alang ng evaluation ang kabuuang optimization workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Constrained Quantum Optimizer implements the Iterative warm-start XY-mixer QAOA(IWS-QAOA) [\\[1\\]](#references). The algorithm runs fixed-angle QAOA circuits on quantum hardware and updates the initial warm-start probabilities of each circuit using measurement outcomes from the previous iteration. No variational parameter training is required; instead, a fixed linear ramp parametrization is chosen.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapatupad ng Constrained Quantum Optimizer ang Iterative warm-start XY-mixer QAOA (IWS-QAOA) [\\[1\\]](#references). Pinapatakbo ng algorithm ang fixed-angle QAOA circuits sa quantum hardware at ina-update ang paunang warm-start probabilities ng bawat circuit gamit ang measurement outcomes mula sa nakaraang iteration. Walang kinakailangang variational parameter training; sa halip, isang fixed linear ramp parametrization ang ginagamit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By using XY-mixers to enforce one-hot constraints, you can drastically improve solution quality for constrained problems, because the search space is practically reduced to a smaller feasible subspace &mdash; and no additional complexity, due to penalty terms, is introduced in the optimization landscape.\n"
msgstr "Sa paggamit ng XY-mixers para i-enforce ang one-hot constraints, malaki ang maitutulong na pagpapabuti sa solution quality para sa mga constrained problem, dahil praktikal na nababawasan ang search space patungo sa mas maliit na feasible subspace &mdash; at walang idinadagdag na komplikasyon, dahil sa penalty terms, sa optimization landscape.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow {#workflow}"
msgstr "Daloy ng Gawain {#workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow of the function is described below:\n"
msgstr "Inilalarawan sa ibaba ang daloy ng gawain ng function:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Preprocessing**: Before circuit synthesis, the optimizer analyzes the constraint structure of the input problem:\n"
msgstr "**Preprocessing**: Bago ang circuit synthesis, sinusuri ng optimizer ang constraint structure ng input problem:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Graph preprocessing:_ When applicable to the problem, it is analyzed as a graph, where edges determine the relationship between variables. This graph analysis enables two preprocessing problem enhancements. First, single constraints can be aggregated to one large constraint by using clique merging, so that they are represented by a single XY-mixer. Second, variables with only a single neighbor can be fixed deterministically, reducing the problem size and complexity.\n"
msgstr "_Graph preprocessing:_ Kapag naaangkop sa problema, sinusuri ito bilang graph, kung saan tinutukoy ng mga edge ang relasyon sa pagitan ng mga variable. Ang graph analysis na ito ay nagbibigay-daan sa dalawang preprocessing enhancement. Una, ang mga single constraint ay maaaring pagsamahin sa isang malaking constraint gamit ang clique merging, para irepresenta ang mga ito ng iisang XY-mixer. Pangalawa, ang mga variable na may iisang neighbor lamang ay maaaring i-fix nang deterministiko, na binabawasan ang laki at komplikasyon ng problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Constraint resolution:_ The preprocessor handles each constraint separately: If the constraint is a one-hot constraint, it can be enforced through XY-mixers. If it is a set-packing constraint, it will first be transformed to a one-hot constraint. Equality constraints are handled through quadratic penalties, and inequality constraints through [unbalanced penalization](https://doi.org/10.1088/2058-9565/ad35e4).\n"
msgstr "_Constraint resolution:_ Hinahawakan ng preprocessor ang bawat constraint nang hiwalay: Kung ang constraint ay one-hot constraint, maaari itong i-enforce sa pamamagitan ng XY-mixers. Kung ito ay set-packing constraint, ito muna ay ikokonberti sa one-hot constraint. Ang equality constraints ay hinahawakan sa pamamagitan ng quadratic penalties, at ang inequality constraints sa pamamagitan ng [unbalanced penalization](https://doi.org/10.1088/2058-9565/ad35e4).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Penalty derivation:_ Constraints that cannot be expressed as one-hot equality constraints are converted to penalty terms. The optimizer derives the penalty strength automatically from the problem structure.\n"
msgstr "_Penalty derivation:_ Ang mga constraint na hindi maipapahayag bilang one-hot equality constraints ay kino-convert sa penalty terms. Awtomatikong kinukuha ng optimizer ang penalty strength batay sa structure ng problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Iterative warm-starting**: The optimizer runs multiple _parallel warm-start chains_. Each chain holds a probability distribution over variable assignments, which is used as the starting probability of the QAOA circuit (warm-start state). At each iteration, a chain samples from the quantum circuit, applies classical postprocessing, and updates its distribution based on the occurrence of samples. Across iterations, this focuses the search on high-quality solutions without a variational optimization loop.\n"
msgstr "**Iterative warm-starting**: Pinapatakbo ng optimizer ang maraming _parallel warm-start chains_. Ang bawat chain ay may hawak na probability distribution sa mga variable assignment, na ginagamit bilang starting probability ng QAOA circuit (warm-start state). Sa bawat iteration, kumukuha ang chain ng samples mula sa quantum circuit, nag-aaplay ng classical postprocessing, at ina-update ang distribution nito batay sa paglitaw ng mga sample. Sa magkakasunod na iteration, tinutuunan nito ang paghahanap sa mga high-quality solution nang walang variational optimization loop.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of chains (`num_parallel`), the total shot budget per chain (`total_shots`), and the number of QAOA repetitions (`reps`) are the primary controls for trading solution quality against runtime.\n"
msgstr "Ang bilang ng chains (`num_parallel`), ang total shot budget kada chain (`total_shots`), at ang bilang ng QAOA repetitions (`reps`) ang pangunahing mga kontrol para sa pagbabalanse ng solution quality laban sa runtime.\n"

