# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 1: A simple constrained problem {#example-1-a-simple-constrained-problem}"
msgstr "Halimbawa 1: Isang simpleng constrained problem {#example-1-a-simple-constrained-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first example shows how to use the function with [LP-files](https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/icos/22.1.1?topic=cplex-lp-file-format-algebraic-representation), a common optimization problem specification used in operations research. You will formulate the following arbitrary optimization problem of five binary variables $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ subject to two constraints:\n"
"$$\n"
"    \\min x_1 x_2 + 2 x_2 x_3 - x_3 x_4 - 2 x_4 x_5 - 2 x_1 x_3 - 4 x_2 x_5 \\\\\n"
"    \\text{s.t.}\\quad x_1 + x_2 + x_3 \\leq 1 \\\\\n"
"    \\quad x_3 - x_4 + x_5 = 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng unang halimbawa kung paano gamitin ang function gamit ang [LP-files](https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/icos/22.1.1?topic=cplex-lp-file-format-algebraic-representation), isang karaniwang optimization problem specification na ginagamit sa operations research. Bubuuin mo ang sumusunod na arbitrary optimization problem na may limang binary variable $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ na napapailalim sa dalawang constraint:\n"
"$$\n"
"    \\min x_1 x_2 + 2 x_2 x_3 - x_3 x_4 - 2 x_4 x_5 - 2 x_1 x_3 - 4 x_2 x_5 \\\\\n"
"    \\text{s.t.}\\quad x_1 + x_2 + x_3 \\leq 1 \\\\\n"
"    \\quad x_3 - x_4 + x_5 = 0\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Formulate the problem {#1-formulate-the-problem}"
msgstr "1. Bumuo ng problema {#1-formulate-the-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Directly state the mathematical expression as the following LP-string format:\n"
msgstr "Direktang isaad ang mathematical expression bilang sumusunod na LP-string format:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that `[ ... ] / 2` is a required notation for quadratic objectives from the LP standard.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang `[ ... ] / 2` ay isang required notation para sa quadratic objectives mula sa LP standard.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Run the optimizer {#2-run-the-optimizer}"
msgstr "2. Patakbuhin ang optimizer {#2-run-the-optimizer}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Solve the problem with the optimizer.\n"
msgstr "Lutasin ang problema gamit ang optimizer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Retrieve the result {#3-retrieve-the-result}"
msgstr "3. Kunin ang resulta {#3-retrieve-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The solution, mapping the variable names to the associated assignments, is provided by the result.\n"
msgstr "Ang solusyon, na nagma-map ng mga pangalan ng variable sa kanilang kaugnay na assignment, ay ibinibigay ng resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `solutions` field in the return dictionary contains all degenerate best solutions found. Alongside the solution data, the `obj_value`, a `feasible` flag, and additional `metadata` are provided.\n"
msgstr "Ang `solutions` field sa return dictionary ay naglalaman ng lahat ng nahanap na degenerate best solutions. Kasama ng solution data, ibinibigay rin ang `obj_value`, isang `feasible` flag, at karagdagang `metadata`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 2: Maximum Independent Set {#example-2-maximum-independent-set}"
msgstr "Halimbawa 2: Maximum Independent Set {#example-2-maximum-independent-set}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Maximum Independent Set (MIS) problem asks for the largest subset of vertices in a graph such that no two vertices in the subset share an edge. This example solves MIS on a 12-node regular graph. For more information on the problem and a larger example, refer to the [tutorial](/tutorials/find-the-maximum-independent-set-with-aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer).\n"
msgstr "Hinahanap ng Maximum Independent Set (MIS) problem ang pinakamalaking subset ng vertices sa isang graph kung saan walang dalawang vertex sa subset ang nagbabahagi ng edge. Nilulutas ng halimbawang ito ang MIS sa 12-node regular graph. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa problema at mas malaking halimbawa, tingnan ang [tutorial](/tutorials/find-the-maximum-independent-set-with-aqarios-constrained-quantum-optimizer).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The problem is built with [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/qiskit/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper).\n"
"Install the required packages if needed:\n"
msgstr ""
"Binuo ang problema gamit ang [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/qiskit/qiskit-addon-opt-mapper).\n"
"I-install ang mga kinakailangang package kung kailangan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Define the problem {#step-1-define-the-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: Tukuyin ang problema {#step-1-define-the-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a random 3-regular graph and create the MIS optimization problem. Each graph node becomes a binary variable, and each edge introduces a constraint ensuring that at most one endpoint is selected.\n"
msgstr "Bumuo ng random 3-regular graph at gumawa ng MIS optimization problem. Ang bawat graph node ay nagiging binary variable, at ang bawat edge ay nagdadala ng constraint na tinitiyak na hanggang isang endpoint lamang ang mapipili.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Run the optimizer {#step-2-run-the-optimizer}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: Patakbuhin ang optimizer {#step-2-run-the-optimizer}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Retrieve and interpret results {#step-3-retrieve-and-interpret-results}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Kunin at bigyang-kahulugan ang mga resulta {#step-3-retrieve-and-interpret-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally we retrieve the solution and verify for correctness.\n"
msgstr "Sa huli, kukunin natin ang solusyon at ve-verify ang katumpakan nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 3: Graph 3-coloring (Max-3-Cut) {#example-3-graph-3-coloring-max-3-cut}"
msgstr "Halimbawa 3: Graph 3-coloring (Max-3-Cut) {#example-3-graph-3-coloring-max-3-cut}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Max-$k$-Cut problem partitions the vertices of a graph into $k$ groups to maximize the number of edges whose endpoints belong to different groups. For $k = 3$ this is equivalent to finding a 3-coloring that maximizes cross-color edges.\n"
msgstr "Hinahati ng Max-$k$-Cut problem ang mga vertex ng graph sa $k$ na grupo para i-maximize ang bilang ng mga edge na ang mga endpoint ay nasa magkaibang grupo. Para sa $k = 3$, katumbas ito ng paghahanap ng 3-coloring na nagpapalaki sa cross-color edges.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formally, assign each node $i \\in V$ to one of $k$ groups with binary variables $x_{i,c}$ for color $c \\in \\{1, \\ldots, k\\}$. The one-hot constraint $\\sum_c x_{i,c} = 1$ for each node enforces a unique assignment. The objective maximizes cross-group edges:\n"
msgstr "Sa pormal na paraan, itinatalaga ang bawat node $i \\in V$ sa isa sa $k$ na grupo gamit ang binary variables $x_{i,c}$ para sa kulay $c \\in \\{1, \\ldots, k\\}$. Ang one-hot constraint $\\sum_c x_{i,c} = 1$ para sa bawat node ay nag-e-enforce ng natatanging assignment. Ang objective ay nagpapalaki sa cross-group edges:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min \\sum_{(u,v) \\in E} \\sum_c x_{u,c} \\, x_{v,c}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\sum_{c} x_{i,c} = 1 \\quad \\forall i \\in  V\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min \\sum_{(u,v) \\in E} \\sum_c x_{u,c} \\, x_{v,c}\\\\\n"
"\\text{s.t.} \\sum_{c} x_{i,c} = 1 \\quad \\forall i \\in  V\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The one-hot constraints are ideal for XY-mixers, which the optimizer handles natively.\n"
msgstr "Ang one-hot constraints ay ideal para sa XY-mixers, na hinahawakan ng optimizer nang natively.\n"

